//
// The decode (aie2_decode.py) at 2 layers on NPU2: up to 4 tokens per
// dispatch, on-chip lm_head + sampler + feedback, growing KV. Every token,
// its record's seed, the last token's final residual and the whole KV cache
// match the numpy oracle. --synthetic-weights swaps the gated Llama
// embedding table for a seeded one with the same layout; the numpy oracle
// runs on that same table. The nightly component check covers the real
// weights at 16 layers. The test compiles the design to a full ELF with
// @iron.jit and dispatches it through pyxrt; every RUN shares that build.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings, xrt_python_ctrl_scratchpad_bo
//
// From an empty cache: the first tokens attend one partial KV block.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 0 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: building synthetic embed/final_norm
// CHECK: KV cache: PASS
// CHECK: final hidden: PASS
// CHECK: chain_persist_grow_mh: 4/4 tokens PASS
//
// Two dispatches crossing a KV block boundary (position 63 to 64), with the
// NPU left idle past its autosuspend delay in between: the KV cache and the
// next seed carry over in DDR.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --dispatches 2 --idle-s 6 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CARRY
// CARRY-COUNT-2: KV cache: PASS
// CARRY: chain_persist_grow_mh: 8/8 tokens PASS
// CARRY: carry across 2 dispatches: PASS
//
// Three of the four token slots, against the same three tokens one per
// dispatch: the records, the KV cache and the stage are byte-identical, and
// the slots that do not run move nothing.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --passes 3 --split | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLIT
// SPLIT: KV cache: PASS
// SPLIT: chain_persist_grow_mh: 3/3 tokens PASS
// SPLIT: 3 tokens vs 3 x 1: PASS
//
// Sampled, with the sampler's settings per dispatch: each token is the
// oracle's draw.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 5 --sample-temp 0.7 --sample-topk 4 --sample-seed 1234 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAMPLE
// SAMPLE-COUNT-4: PASS {{.*}} [sampled]
// SAMPLE: final hidden: PASS
// SAMPLE: chain_persist_grow_mh: 4/4 tokens PASS
//
// A 7-token prompt, then generation: the prompt runs in batches of up to 4
// tokens, a dispatch each, every batch row's input the seed the device
// makes of its embed row; the batch before the last skips the lm_head and
// leaves the records untouched, and the batches do not cross a KV block.
// The same prompt a token per dispatch leaves byte-identical sampled
// records, KV cache, final residuals (the prompt's last and the run's) and
// seed.
// RUN: env LLAMA_CHAIN_N=2 %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_chain_persist_grow_mh.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 60 --prompt-tokens 7 --vs-batch 1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PROMPT
// PROMPT-COUNT-4: prompt, no sample
// PROMPT: KV cache: PASS
// PROMPT: final hidden: PASS
// PROMPT: records: untouched
// PROMPT-COUNT-2: prompt, no sample
// PROMPT-COUNT-2: KV cache: PASS
// PROMPT-COUNT-5: batches of 4 vs 1, {{.*}}: same
// PROMPT: chain_persist_grow_mh: 5/5 tokens PASS
// PROMPT: carry across 3 dispatches: PASS
// PROMPT: prompt in batches of 4 vs 1: PASS
